        "date_published": "2026-02-05T08:46:13+00:00",
        "description": "<p>This is a little game implemented over a week of tinkering and targeting Emacs.<p>The point is both to have fun with this kind of simulations, and also explore the \"functional core / imperative shell\" approach to architecture. I also developed a tile and tile effect definition DSL, which makes this even easier to extend. From this point of view it's a success: easy testing, easy extension,<p>Gameplay-wise the simulation is too simplistic, and needs input from people interested in this kind of toys. The original Micropolis/SimSity is the last time I built a virtual city.</p>\n<hr>\n<p>Comments URL: <a href=\"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=46897332\">https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=46897332</a></p>\n<p>Points: 8</p>\n<p># Comments: 3</p>",
